   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Newborn with ambiguous genitalia: KARYOTYPE first",
   "lines": [
    "disorder of sexual development (DSD) = discrepancy between karyotype, gonads, internal and external genitalia · 1 in 4,500 births",
    "karyotype + pelvic/abdominal ultrasound in every case, then labs by your differential",
    "not always ambiguous genitalia: may present as abnormal puberty · gender identity, expression and sexual orientation are out of scope"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g1",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 192,
   "w": 780,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "46,XY DSD: under-virilised",
   "lines": [
    "gonads: TESTES · external genitalia incompletely virilised"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g2",
   "x": 865,
   "y": 192,
   "w": 780,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "46,XX DSD: virilised",
   "lines": [
    "gonads: OVARIES · external genitalia virilised by increased fetal androgen"
   ]
  },
